{"Title":"An Act promoting personal access of driving records","BillNumber":"H3381","DocketNumber":"HD1234","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T11:56:50.737"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T11:56:50.7366667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3381/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative McMurtry of Dedham, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3381) of Paul McMurtry that the Registrar of Motor Vehicles be authorized to make driving records available online for informational purposes.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1.  Section 1A of Chapter 90 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2014 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following paragraph:- The registrar shall make a person’s driving records available online for informational purposes.  Such records shall be considered unattested and need not be certified with the signature of the registrar, but shall include any suspensions, outstanding tickets or other citations issued to the driver.  Such records shall be updated regularly to reflect the most accurate information available, consistent with the way in which attested driving records are maintained for law enforcement agencies.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}